        "implementation": "cpp",
        "sourceFile": "SDO_WRITE_DATA.cpp",
        "documentation": "Writes the first DATALENGTH bytes (1 to 256) of the byte array DATA to an object of a node by SDO. Handshake as SDO_WRITE4. NETWORK counts from 1; DEVICE is the node ID or its name; TIMEOUT T#0s uses the network SDO timeout.\nExample: write(ENABLE := set, DEVICE := IO_Module, INDEX := 16#2000, SUBINDEX := 0, DATALENGTH := 6, DATA := bytes);"
      },
