        "inouts": [],
        "implementation": "cpp",
        "sourceFile": "NMT.cpp",
        "documentation": "Sends an NMT command to a node, or with DEVICE 0 to every node of the network: STATE is START_REMOTE_NODE, STOP_REMOTE_NODE, ENTER_PRE_OPERATIONAL, RESET_NODE or RESET_COMMUNICATION. A node stopped or set pre-operational this way is not a node loss; a start returns it to operational. A rising edge of ENABLE sends it; CONFIRM once sent. TIMEOUT is not used (NMT has no answer).\nExample: nmt(ENABLE := restart, DEVICE := IO_Module, STATE := START_REMOTE_NODE);"
      },
      {
