          }
        ],
        "outputs": [
          {
            "name": "CONFIRM",
            "type": "BOOL"
          },
          {
            "name": "ERROR",
            "type": "USINT"
          },
          {
            "name": "ERRORTEXT",
            "type": "STRING"
          },
          {
            "name": "EMCY",
            "type": "EMCY_ERROR"
          }
        ],
        "inouts": [],
        "implementation": "cpp",
        "sourceFile": "RECV_EMCY_DEV.cpp",
        "documentation": "Returns one node's emergency messages one per call while ENABLE is TRUE, oldest first: CONFIRM is TRUE in a call that returns one, with the message in EMCY. Messages from before the instance's first call are skipped; each instance has its own position. NETWORK counts from 1; DEVICE is the node ID or its name.\nExample: emcy(ENABLE := TRUE, DEVICE := IO_Module); IF emcy.CONFIRM AND emcy.EMCY.ERRORCODE <> 0 THEN alarm := TRUE; END_IF;"
      },
      {
        "name": "CANOPEN_NODE_ENABLE",
        "inputs": [
          {
            "name": "NETWORK",
            "type": "USINT"
          },
          {
            "name": "ENABLE",
            "type": "BOOL"
          },
          {
            "name": "DEVICE",
            "type": "USINT"
          },
          {
            "name": "ACTIVE",
            "type": "BOOL"
          }
        ],
        "outputs": [
          {
            "name": "CONFIRM",
            "type": "BOOL"
          },
          {
            "name": "BUSY",
            "type": "BOOL"
          },
          {
            "name": "ERROR",
            "type": "USINT"
          },
          {
            "name": "ERRORTEXT",
            "type": "STRING"
          }
        ],
        "inouts": [],
        "implementation": "cpp",
        "sourceFile": "CANOPEN_NODE_ENABLE.cpp",
        "documentation": "Turns a node on or off while the PLC runs: while ENABLE is TRUE the node is on when ACTIVE is TRUE and off when it is FALSE. Each change of ACTIVE sends one request; BUSY until the master has applied it, then CONFIRM. A node that is off is not booted, supervised or warned about and gets no PDOs; turning off a running node sends it NMT stop and handles its inputs as on a loss. The choice lasts until the PLC stops; at the next start the node's \"On at PLC start\" setting applies again. NETWORK counts from 1; DEVICE is the node ID or its name.\nExample: gripper(ENABLE := TRUE, DEVICE := Gripper, ACTIVE := has_gripper);"
      },
      {
        "name": "CANOPEN_NODE_STATUS",
        "inputs": [
          {
            "name": "NETWORK",
            "type": "USINT"
          },
          {
            "name": "ENABLE",
