            "name": "FAULTY",
            "type": "USINT"
          }
        ],
        "inouts": [],
        "implementation": "cpp",
        "sourceFile": "CANOPEN_NETWORK_STATE.cpp",
        "documentation": "Gives the state of a whole network, in the same call while ENABLE is TRUE: MANDATORY_UP when every mandatory node that is on is operational or waits for the program's start, OPTIONAL_UP the same for the optional nodes, and the number of nodes CONFIGURED (operational, waiting or set by hand), OPERATIONAL, WAITING for the program's start, DISABLED (off) and FAULTY (failed, lost, held, or mandatory and not answering). Nodes that are off count in neither flag. NETWORK counts from 1.\nExample: net(ENABLE := TRUE); IF net.MANDATORY_UP THEN start(ENABLE := TRUE, DEVICE := IO_Module, STATE := START_REMOTE_NODE); END_IF;"
      },
