        "implementation": "cpp",
        "sourceFile": "CANOPEN_SLAVE_STATUS.cpp",
        "documentation": "Gives the state of this runtime's CANopen slave, in the same call while ENABLE is TRUE: STATE (PRE_OPERATIONAL, OPERATIONAL, STOPPED, or NOT_AVAIL while its interface is not open), OPERATIONAL, the node ID in use in NODEID, whether the master's heartbeat is watched (MASTERWATCHED) and received (MASTERSEEN), the link in BUSSTATE (BUS_ERROR_ACTIVE, BUS_ERROR_PASSIVE, BUS_OFF or BUS_UNKNOWN), the error register 0x1001 in ERRORREGISTER and the number of active emergencies in EMCYACTIVE. The values are at most 100 ms old. SLAVE is the slave's name or its place in the project's slaves, from 1.\nExample: slave(SLAVE := Line_IO, ENABLE := TRUE); IF NOT slave.MASTERSEEN THEN ... END_IF;"
      },
      {
        "name": "CANOPEN_SLAVE_NMT",
        "inputs": [
          {
            "name": "SLAVE",
            "type": "USINT"
          },
          {
            "name": "ENABLE",
            "type": "BOOL"
          },
          {
            "name": "STATE",
            "type": "USINT"
          }
        ],
        "outputs": [
          {
            "name": "CONFIRM",
            "type": "BOOL"
          },
          {
            "name": "BUSY",
            "type": "BOOL"
          },
          {
            "name": "ERROR",
            "type": "USINT"
          },
          {
            "name": "ERRORTEXT",
            "type": "STRING"
          }
        ],
        "inouts": [],
        "implementation": "cpp",
        "sourceFile": "CANOPEN_SLAVE_NMT.cpp",
        "documentation": "Puts this runtime's CANopen slave into an NMT state by itself (CiA 301 local control): STATE is START_REMOTE_NODE, STOP_REMOTE_NODE or ENTER_PRE_OPERATIONAL; a reset is refused. A rising edge of ENABLE sends it; BUSY until the slave is in that state, then CONFIRM. The master sees a slave that leaves operational this way as left operational and acts on its own settings; raise an emergency first so it knows why. SLAVE is the slave's name or its place in the project's slaves, from 1.\nExample: nmt(SLAVE := Line_IO, ENABLE := fault, STATE := ENTER_PRE_OPERATIONAL);"
      },
      {
        "name": "CANOPEN_SLAVE_EMCY",
        "inputs": [
          {
            "name": "SLAVE",
            "type": "USINT"
          },
          {
            "name": "ENABLE",
            "type": "BOOL"
          },
          {
            "name": "ERRORCODE",
            "type": "WORD"
          },
          {
            "name": "INFO",
            "type": "UDINT"
          }
        ],
        "outputs": [
          {
            "name": "CONFIRM",
            "type": "BOOL"
          },
          {
            "name": "ERROR",
            "type": "USINT"
          },
          {
            "name": "ERRORTEXT",
            "type": "STRING"
          },
          {
            "name": "ACTIVE",
            "type": "BOOL"
          }
        ],
        "inouts": [],
        "implementation": "cpp",
        "sourceFile": "CANOPEN_SLAVE_EMCY.cpp",
        "documentation": "Holds one emergency of the program on this runtime's CANopen slave: while ENABLE is TRUE it is active with ERRORCODE and INFO (sent in bytes 4 to 7 of the EMCY); ENABLE FALSE clears it, and the slave sends EMCY 0000h once no emergency is left. A change of ERRORCODE or INFO while active sends one more EMCY, so do not change them every scan. The error register gets the generic bit and the bit of the code's class (2xxx current, 3xxx voltage, 4xxx temperature, 8xxx communication, FFxx manufacturer). Each instance holds one emergency, up to 31 per slave; 0000h, 6200h and 8130h are the slave's own and refused. A PLC stop clears them; after the start the block raises its emergency again. SLAVE is the slave's name or its place in the project's slaves, from 1.\nExample: overheat(SLAVE := Line_IO, ENABLE := temp > 80.0, ERRORCODE := 16#4210, INFO := REAL_TO_UDINT(temp * 10.0));"
      },
      {
        "name": "CANOPEN_SLAVE_WRITTEN",
        "inputs": [
          {
            "name": "SLAVE",
            "type": "USINT"
          },
          {
            "name": "ENABLE",
            "type": "BOOL"
          },
          {
            "name": "INDEX",
            "type": "WORD"
          },
          {
            "name": "SUBINDEX",
            "type": "BYTE"
          }
        ],
        "outputs": [
          {
            "name": "CONFIRM",
            "type": "BOOL"
          },
          {
            "name": "ERROR",
            "type": "USINT"
          },
          {
            "name": "ERRORTEXT",
            "type": "STRING"
          },
          {
            "name": "COUNT",
            "type": "UDINT"
          },
          {
            "name": "NEW",
            "type": "BOOL"
          }
        ],
        "inouts": [],
        "implementation": "cpp",
        "sourceFile": "CANOPEN_SLAVE_WRITTEN.cpp",
        "documentation": "Tells how often the master has written an object of this runtime's CANopen slave, by SDO or RPDO, also with the same value: COUNT since the slave started, and NEW TRUE in the call after COUNT changed (in the first call when it was written before). An object mapped to an RPDO counts every frame. INDEX and SUBINDEX name an object from the master. SLAVE is the slave's name or its place in the project's slaves, from 1.\nExample: cmd(SLAVE := Line_IO, ENABLE := TRUE, INDEX := 16#2000, SUBINDEX := 1); IF cmd.NEW THEN ... END_IF;"
      }
    ],
    "types": [
      {
        "name": "CANOPEN_KERNEL_ERROR",
        "kind": "alias",
        "documentation": "The ERROR of the blocks (USINT): CANOPEN_KERNEL_NO_ERROR, _OTHER_ERROR (the node aborted, see ERRORINFO), _TIMEOUT, _BUS_OFF, _ERROR_PASSIVE, _INTERNAL, _WRONG_PARAMETER, _NODE_ID_UNKNOWN, _NET_ID_UNKNOWN, _REQUEST_ERROR, _NO_DRIVER."
      },
      {
        "name": "DEVICE_STATE",
        "kind": "alias",
        "documentation": "The STATE of GET_STATE and CANOPEN_SLAVE_STATUS (USINT): INIT, RESET_COMM, RESET_APP, PRE_OPERATIONAL, STOPPED, OPERATIONAL, UNKNOWN, NOT_AVAIL."
      },
      {
        "name": "TRANSITION_STATE",
        "kind": "alias",
        "documentation": "The STATE of NMT (USINT): START_REMOTE_NODE, STOP_REMOTE_NODE, ENTER_PRE_OPERATIONAL, RESET_NODE, RESET_COMMUNICATION. CANOPEN_SLAVE_NMT takes the first three."
      },
      {
        "name": "CANOPEN_RUN_STATE",
        "kind": "alias",
        "documentation": "The RUNSTATE of CANOPEN_NODE_STATUS (USINT): RUN_NOT_FOUND (not booted yet), RUN_BOOTING, RUN_FAILED (the last boot failed, retried in the background), RUN_WAITING_START (configured, waits for the program's NMT start), RUN_OPERATIONAL, RUN_MANUAL (stopped or pre-operational by an NMT command), RUN_LOST, RUN_HELD (lost and stopped until the next PLC start), RUN_DISABLED (off), RUN_STOPPED (the PLC stopped)."
      },
      {
        "name": "CANOPEN_BUS_STATE",
        "kind": "alias",
        "documentation": "The BUSSTATE of CANOPEN_SLAVE_STATUS (USINT): BUS_ERROR_ACTIVE (the link is fine), BUS_ERROR_PASSIVE, BUS_OFF, BUS_UNKNOWN."
      },
      {
        "name": "EMCY_ERROR",
        "kind": "struct",
        "fields": [
          {
            "name": "ERRORCODE",
            "type": "WORD"
          },
          {
            "name": "ERRORREGISTER",
            "type": "BYTE"
          },
          {
            "name": "MANUFACTURERERROR",
            "type": "__INLINE_ARRAY_BYTE"
          }
        ],
        "documentation": "One emergency message: ERRORCODE, ERRORREGISTER and the five MANUFACTURERERROR bytes."
      }
    ],
